    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0096" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg24"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Hr. Hall to Mr. Hunter</hi>.</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Cochabamba, Bolivia</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-24">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 41.]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    circular No. 29, apprising me of the horrible assassination of the late
                    President Lincoln. The news of that deplorable event was received here a
                    fortnight ago, through the Panama papers, and produced a sensation of universal
                    and deep regret. From the inhabitants of this city I have received many
                    expressions of sympathy and condolence. The instructions accompanying the
                    circular that all officers and others subject to the orders of the Secretary of
                    State wear crape upon the left arm for the period of six months,” will be
                    carefully regarded by me.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALLEN A. HALL.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hunter</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
